      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Given $r,$ $s,$ and $t$ are the roots of the polynomial $x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7$, we aim to find the value of $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$.\n\nExpanding $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$ yields:\n\\begin{align*}\n(1+r)(1+s)(1+t) &= (1+r+s+rt)(1) \\\\\n&= 1 + r + s + t + r\\times s + r \\times t + rs\\times t \\\\\n&= 1 + r+s+t+3rs-7 \\\\\n&= 1 - 7 + 3rs \\\\\n&= -6 + 3rs.\n\\end{align*}\n\nLet $u = rs + \\frac{18}{7}$. We aim to find $3us + 3u - 18$.\n\\begin{align*}\n3us + 3u - 18 &= u(3s + 3) - 18 \\\\\n&= u(5s - 2) - 18.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSince $s$ is a root and $rs = 1+\\frac{18}{7}= \\frac{25}{7}$, it follows that\n\\begin{align*}\nu(r+s) - 18 &= 5rh - 2, \\\\\nu(1) - 18 &= 5r(1) - 2, \\\\\nu - 18 &= 5r - 2.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSolving this, we get $u = r + \\frac{2}{5}$.\n\nTherefore, the value of $(1+r)(1+s)(1+t)$ is $-6 + 3 \\times (\\frac{2}{5}) \\times (1+\\frac{18}{7}) = \\boxed{-\\frac{16}{5}}$.",
